steps.evidence:
lock-state 'locked' at boot. /unlock showed the passphrase view with no legal view (shots/T-T1-unlock-en.png), and the unlock landed on /#home. After 8 s with no clicks:
- no guide wizard and no open dialog;
- plane fill=currentColor with class off, body.net-offline;
- top bar box-shadow 'rgb(192,57,43) 0 -2px 0 0 inset' (the red bottom edge);
- /api/system/network online:false;
- the coach is showing (shots/T-T1-home-en.png).

Feed lists 20 synthetic articles (shots/T-T1-feed-en.png). walk1.json steps.T1.

The coach text is exact: 'You're offline. Switch off airplane mode to go online and start collecting.' / 'You'll confirm before anything connects.'. It is now an in-flow strip under the top bar. 'Not now' is on the left (x=1237) and 'Go online' on the right (x=1323), and both buttons are unclassed.

In Ink, Paper, Solar and Mint the computed-style diff between the two buttons is EMPTY:
- the same background (Ink rgb(91,157,217), Paper rgb(154,106,47), Solar rgb(181,137,0), Mint rgb(46,125,91));
- the same text colour;
- weight 600, 12px, height 28;
- border 0 on all sides, no outline, opacity 1.

Only the widths differ (Ink 78.08 vs 85.97 px). The walk finished on Ink ((root ink)). shots/T-T2-coach-{ink,paper,solar,mint}.png, walk1.json T2.

Paper theme, live switches through #lang-switch:
- fr 'Plus tard' / 'Passer en ligne';
- ar 'ليس الآن' / 'الاتصال';
- zh '暂不' / '联网'.

Both sentences match the locale files exactly in all three (expected_ok all true), and the button style diff is [] in every language. In ar dir=rtl and the page mirrors. The coach re-anchors on the live switch: in ar the plane is at x 186-220 and the arrow at 203; in zh and en the plane is at 1220-1254 and the arrow at 1237. The arrow is 21 px from the plane, and no top-bar, sidebar or subtab control is covered (covered=[]). shots/T-T3-coach-{fr,ar,zh,en-back}.png.

The coach's 'Go online' opened #net-consent once (open counter 1): title 'Go online?', reason 'Allow network requests again', ifaces 'eth0: 192.0.2.2'. /api/system/network stayed online:false while it was open. The popup's own buttons stay unequal as intended: 'Stay offline' has class secondary and weight 500, 'Go online' is unclassed with weight 600.

After 'Stay offline':
- the coach is gone and oo_net_coach_v1 = {seen:1, dismissed:true};
- the plane is still filled and the red top-bar edge is still there;
- there is no toast;
- network online:false.

shots/T-T4-consent-en.png, shots/T-T4-after-stay-offline-en.png.

Start state: maximum, class rate-max, needle rotate(48), accent colour. The hover is exact.

Click 1:
- needle rotate(-48), accent gone;
- toast 'Collection speed set to the 500 KiB/s target — applies from the next pass.';
- /api/scheduler/config target/500;
- Settings > Advanced > Collection > Advanced (legacy) shows '500 kbps' with the slider at value 2 (3rd of 7);
- the bubble under the pointer shows the new state at once.

Click 2:
- toast 'Collection speed set to Maximum — applies from the next pass.';
- Settings 'Maximum' with the slider at 6;
- config maximum.

The #net-consent open counter stayed at 0, and the app stayed offline. Settings > Wikipedia and > OpenStreetMap have no range or number input and no speed or bandwidth text. The fr, ar and zh hovers and both toasts equal the locale values. KiB/s vs kbps is the known item. shots/T-T6-*.png, walk1.json T6.

Home at 375x812:
- overflow 0 in en and ar;
- #home-tier spans 37-338 px and is 43 px tall, and its caveat 'thin evidence — read with care' is fully visible;
- every row-T top-bar control is in view and clickable;
- the coach sits inside the viewport under the chrome with equal, unclipped buttons, and covers nothing (covered=[]), including palette rows.

/tasks at 375: overflow 0 in en, ar and zh. #tm-tabs scrolls in its own 335 px box (overflow-x:auto), and the last tab 'Sessions' can be clicked. shots/T-375-*.png, walk375.json.

